⚠ First — your two docs contradict each other at GDS 7

Hardware Integration: "Discontinued: Patient no longer interacts with the application or devices directly."

stages.txt: "the auditory cortex and musical memory networks are highly resilient and remain intact even in severe dementia… placed near the bed to play culturally familiar NER folk songs, prayers, or soothing regional sounds… proven to significantly reduce severe physical agitation."

Your Care Guide independently backs the second: "musical memory networks remain remarkably well-preserved even in severe AD, largely escaping early cortical atrophy."

Resolution — and this is the correct synthesis:

▎ Patient interaction discontinues at GDS 7. Patient audio does not.

The hardware doc was reasoning about touchscreens and wearables and over-generalized to "the app." Two of your three docs say the single most effective late-stage intervention is ambient culturally-familiar sound. The app doesn't stop — it stops having a screen.

